[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-39205"] :question/problem "If $u=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,,$ $v=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,,$ and $u\\cdot u=15,$ then $\\frac{u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}u)}{u\\cdot (\\frac{3}{4}v)}=$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the fact that the dot product is linear.\n\nTo quickly compute the numerator $u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}u),$ we multiply $u\\cdot u$ by $\\frac{1}{2}.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}u) & =\\frac{1}{2}(u\\cdot u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 15 \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo quickly compute the denominator $u\\cdot (\\frac{3}{4}v),$ we compute $u\\cdot v$ first and then multiply the result by $\\frac{3}{4}.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot (\\frac{3}{4}v) & =\\frac{3}{4}(u\\cdot v) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}({u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}((-1)\\cdot (-3)+(-3)\\cdot (-1)+(-2)\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}(3+3+4+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}u)}{u\\cdot (\\frac{3}{4}v)} & =\\frac{(\\frac{15}{2})}{9}=\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-40108/selection/89e34329534b6ee904fc166b9ee2a8f587c79161a7c80fc821ab136e40774c36" :answer/id #uuid "0d24c348-49e2-5257-bccf-3ffdf19f8399" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40108/selection/6a53b290f6986792b902511fdb10a5d1da6a43722d885c1ec7c07997890a8d62" :answer/id #uuid "e9297d59-3ecd-5463-aa95-1b61de806491" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40108/selection/cd0bc843a029f1a38bdde9c2ac61776f7a2770c1dabb40a4686183a9adc6f2f0" :answer/id #uuid "610b3919-5214-5467-979e-e521ef8fe497" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{18}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40108/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "67c63fc3-637a-54db-8a75-89d1cd0ab0d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40108/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "2a074d48-c666-5cc9-97fd-19bd3599acbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40108/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cc880282-2206-55e8-851f-465458cf65cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40108/selection/6a53b290f6986792b902511fdb10a5d1da6a43722d885c1ec7c07997890a8d62" :answer-field/choices ["q-40108/selection/89e34329534b6ee904fc166b9ee2a8f587c79161a7c80fc821ab136e40774c36" "q-40108/selection/6a53b290f6986792b902511fdb10a5d1da6a43722d885c1ec7c07997890a8d62" "q-40108/selection/cd0bc843a029f1a38bdde9c2ac61776f7a2770c1dabb40a4686183a9adc6f2f0" "q-40108/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-40108/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40108" :question/id #uuid "7d7c48e0-b3db-50af-b914-55f8cb8435f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-40108" :question/problem "If $u=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,,$ $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\,,$ and $u\\cdot u=17,$ then $\\frac{u\\cdot (2u)}{u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3}v)}=$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the fact that the dot product is linear.\n\nTo quickly compute the numerator $u\\cdot (2u),$ we multiply $u\\cdot u$ by $2.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot (2u) & =2(u\\cdot u) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 17 \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo quickly compute the denominator $u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3}v),$ we compute $u\\cdot v$ first and then multiply the result by $\\frac{1}{3}.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3}v) & =\\frac{1}{3}({u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}((0)\\cdot (1)+3\\cdot (-4)+2\\cdot 2+2\\cdot (-5)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(0-12+4-10) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-18) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{u\\cdot (2u)}{u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3}v)}=\\frac{34}{-6}=-\\frac{17}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-40108/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98eb5973-f9b1-5c2f-8763-e8f8707e9b89"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40108"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-139948/selection/3a9a70c07caaaef6e3dcae1453de98899e541b60c951a35187d3bf1c3dc6e44c" :answer/id #uuid "f0c606fc-97c9-5343-87fc-60d3dab583e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{34}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139948/selection/bc8ddfe9b0ae9ecd586464d3b828bfdd8a405438588d3184601cef690877fd8c" :answer/id #uuid "ec3e3dfe-3432-5581-a312-a50cbae61eda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-34" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139948/selection/ebafed68ffac4e0382e8200bf54f9e61a39537ebcd6d6687003aa58e3b97aa90" :answer/id #uuid "00b360d1-ea2e-5ef9-8311-da8f3ccf2152" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139948/selection/59552bcb3d87e05f7fc53fa78ea3f164a56017eafe3545446ef16fd16689ded1" :answer/id #uuid "1a7b89fa-b259-589b-9fe4-16a0463e92d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139948/selection/ec90217e87a82dbd19a5bccff629cab519a1db16171898967c9251f2b0539fcd" :answer/id #uuid "7e754999-1912-52f7-a5f3-9949f2c1c868" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{17}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139948/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b5473c63-f1e1-520f-a85c-620d7704c9fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-139948/selection/ec90217e87a82dbd19a5bccff629cab519a1db16171898967c9251f2b0539fcd" :answer-field/choices ["q-139948/selection/3a9a70c07caaaef6e3dcae1453de98899e541b60c951a35187d3bf1c3dc6e44c" "q-139948/selection/bc8ddfe9b0ae9ecd586464d3b828bfdd8a405438588d3184601cef690877fd8c" "q-139948/selection/ebafed68ffac4e0382e8200bf54f9e61a39537ebcd6d6687003aa58e3b97aa90" "q-139948/selection/59552bcb3d87e05f7fc53fa78ea3f164a56017eafe3545446ef16fd16689ded1" "q-139948/selection/ec90217e87a82dbd19a5bccff629cab519a1db16171898967c9251f2b0539fcd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-139948" :question/id #uuid "c6000e94-92ff-51a9-88f5-c3892fb8a07e" :question/math-academy-id "q-139948" :question/problem "If $u=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,,$ $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\,,$ and $u\\cdot v=-1,$ then $\\frac{(5u)\\cdot v}{v\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}v)}=$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the fact that the dot product is linear.\n\nTo quickly compute the numerator $(5u)\\cdot v,$ we multiply $u\\cdot v$ by $5.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5u)\\cdot v & =5(u\\cdot v) \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo quickly compute the denominator $v\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}v),$ we compute $v\\cdot v$ first and then multiply the result by $\\frac{1}{2}.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}v) & =\\frac{1}{2}(v\\cdot v) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}+{v}_{5}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{5}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+4+4+0+25) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 34 \\\\  & =17.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{(5u)\\cdot v}{v\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}v)}=-\\frac{5}{17}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-139948/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98eb5973-f9b1-5c2f-8763-e8f8707e9b89"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-139948"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74040/selection/1f5b353af7cbb90a89e4a07f196cff5b0ba27d9934d00e9a38de61eff80108f7" :answer/id #uuid "392050f8-43d5-5087-a20a-aed076684727" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74040/selection/d6944c4d51ee6e8916d5e2815a8478bad91a2f9e9e9bcd499b503b9fbcb165ab" :answer/id #uuid "263f9988-fde7-53ea-9d3a-f9024d34bd61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "54" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74040/selection/127702955aa9819583fc274bc6829ce2debf65f2652590094119a1bfcc1b42d5" :answer/id #uuid "0a735ea3-faa6-5228-bcd5-04ec1d804935" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74040/selection/348574193cea2f1b2a034c12a816bed437c8e13e962a44351f17e519b320f847" :answer/id #uuid "b3eaba96-25bd-5912-b566-c451424a631e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{27}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74040/selection/74dee60e2d310a70b6506a0bbb9d1a5efe998972e06348f66a7e85d3fd6c23dd" :answer/id #uuid "bf7e8d07-1661-5112-8160-d9ce6a62e209" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74040/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "58bf06f6-3da9-53d8-b77d-21710c893510" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74040/selection/127702955aa9819583fc274bc6829ce2debf65f2652590094119a1bfcc1b42d5" :answer-field/choices ["q-74040/selection/1f5b353af7cbb90a89e4a07f196cff5b0ba27d9934d00e9a38de61eff80108f7" "q-74040/selection/d6944c4d51ee6e8916d5e2815a8478bad91a2f9e9e9bcd499b503b9fbcb165ab" "q-74040/selection/127702955aa9819583fc274bc6829ce2debf65f2652590094119a1bfcc1b42d5" "q-74040/selection/348574193cea2f1b2a034c12a816bed437c8e13e962a44351f17e519b320f847" "q-74040/selection/74dee60e2d310a70b6506a0bbb9d1a5efe998972e06348f66a7e85d3fd6c23dd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74040" :question/id #uuid "205a52bf-ab3a-51fb-bc92-9d8428f733fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-74040" :question/problem "If $u=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\,,$ $v=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,,$ and $u\\cdot u=27,$ then $\\frac{(2u)\\cdot u}{u\\cdot (3v)}=$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the fact that the dot product is linear.\n\nTo quickly compute the numerator $(2u)\\cdot u,$ we multiply $u\\cdot u$ by $2.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2u)\\cdot u & =2(u\\cdot u) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 27 \\\\  & =54.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo quickly compute the denominator $u\\cdot (3v),$ we compute $u\\cdot v$ first and then multiply the result by $3.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot (3v) & =3(u\\cdot v) \\\\  & =3({u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4}) \\\\  & =3(2\\cdot (-3)+3\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot (-1)+(-2)\\cdot 3+(-3)\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =3(-6-6-1-6-6) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-25) \\\\  & =-75.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{(2u)\\cdot u}{u\\cdot (3v)}=\\frac{54}{-75}=-\\frac{18}{25}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-74040/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98eb5973-f9b1-5c2f-8763-e8f8707e9b89"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74040"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74039/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer/id #uuid "6d5001dd-7501-5b26-964c-f5835c939b2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74039/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "66937c48-e6cd-5956-acc0-776bacd8cab7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74039/selection/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "3a532d6e-e8e3-532f-8f31-5d9ac4a34a2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74039/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" :answer/id #uuid "3de4debd-54c2-5b5f-9c6d-4eca0da83549" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74039/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "385a43c9-b970-551a-8472-e1ecb7db128c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74039/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "27993627-a4aa-5611-9862-8acc6672f405" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74039/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" :answer-field/choices ["q-74039/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" "q-74039/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-74039/selection/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" "q-74039/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" "q-74039/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74039" :question/id #uuid "526891b7-386c-5932-bad3-5b20c2a854b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-74039" :question/problem "If $u=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\,,$ $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\,,$ and $u\\cdot u=30,$ then $\\frac{(\\frac{2}{3}u)\\cdot u}{u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}v)}=$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the fact that the dot product is linear.\n\nTo quickly compute the numerator $(\\frac{2}{3}u)\\cdot u,$ we multiply $u\\cdot u$ by $\\frac{2}{3}.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{2}{3}u)\\cdot u & =\\frac{2}{3}(u\\cdot u) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 30 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo quickly compute the denominator $u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}v),$ we compute $u\\cdot v$ first and then multiply the result by $\\frac{1}{2}.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}v) & =\\frac{1}{2}(u\\cdot v) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 2+3\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+2+0-3-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{(\\frac{2}{3}u)\\cdot u}{u\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}v)}=\\frac{20}{-2}=-10.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-74039/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98eb5973-f9b1-5c2f-8763-e8f8707e9b89"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74039"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-39196/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer/id #uuid "0fbbdfb5-230c-5c60-b459-60d2ec3363e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39196/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "a84b8796-cf7c-5a2e-a6e6-4ac46c5c11d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39196/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "c7c8ce62-97dd-5003-8fbc-ffbb8e479943" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39196/selection/abe476e447976564bc5c670fe73789666287b967d49bbed12b1d85144449e63e" :answer/id #uuid "7f311bdb-932e-525d-b167-524fe1dd8aee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "23" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39196/selection/2fa5baf88b61736a3022c72e24e172fda2b4270fffff6efaa1fc03fef23fccc2" :answer/id #uuid "41202990-aff1-56c0-a0af-9777c22a5773" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39196/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "77e50938-562f-5646-9e91-fdd629f75ee3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-39196/selection/2fa5baf88b61736a3022c72e24e172fda2b4270fffff6efaa1fc03fef23fccc2" :answer-field/choices ["q-39196/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" "q-39196/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-39196/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-39196/selection/abe476e447976564bc5c670fe73789666287b967d49bbed12b1d85144449e63e" "q-39196/selection/2fa5baf88b61736a3022c72e24e172fda2b4270fffff6efaa1fc03fef23fccc2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-39196" :question/id #uuid "34af850c-ea7c-55c3-b564-f39c0446abaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-39196" :question/problem "Find $(2a+5b)\\cdot c+(b+3c)\\cdot d,$ if $c\\cdot a=2,$ $b\\cdot c=3,$ $b\\cdot d=4$ and $d\\cdot c=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that the dot product is linear in the first variable, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2a+5b)\\cdot c+(b+3c)\\cdot d & =(2a)\\cdot c+(5b)\\cdot c+b\\cdot d+(3c)\\cdot d \\\\  & =2(a\\cdot c)+5(b\\cdot c)+b\\cdot d+3(c\\cdot d).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we can use the fact that the dot product is symmetric to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(a\\cdot c)+5(b\\cdot c)+b\\cdot d+3(c\\cdot d) & =2(c\\cdot a)+5(b\\cdot c)+b\\cdot d+3(d\\cdot c).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the values for $c\\cdot a,$ $b\\cdot c,$ $b\\cdot d,$ and $d\\cdot c,$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(c\\cdot a)+5(b\\cdot c)+b\\cdot d+3(d\\cdot c) & =2(2)+5(3)+4+3(1) \\\\  & =4+15+4+3 \\\\  & =26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $(2a+5b)\\cdot c+(b+3c)\\cdot d=26.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-39196/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fba8401-2da1-50f2-8e96-84cbe06d95fc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-39196"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-139951/selection/695792c47319cb1ed098a6d83038b7ad6d032838f9103d693bf346f1dc234ff8" :answer/id #uuid "f9dbe92e-d70b-5239-a9a6-8f4cf1b2b356" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139951/selection/faf6532f0d4ab903ddc295ac11018acfd3bce2ae030f3f2eed578181eeb5e5e5" :answer/id #uuid "7b991c0b-43e5-5e40-a38c-b7af7ae0c330" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139951/selection/ebfc0e0786b9e08f32fe2539ae50e791a60b7c4613bb2a0820cefbd3ea742454" :answer/id #uuid "b9348e5a-fa20-5d2c-aa0b-c02382e777f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139951/selection/bdda2450817a39aa33f63c44268d508ac25aa607d31de284a7a3098288a61525" :answer/id #uuid "0f940e14-8e0a-5a6a-83f2-bcb09c778b6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "72" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139951/selection/95f0217cc1a787fa427ae3652ee08f6e7e92976368d3018500a5edad740eb418" :answer/id #uuid "e358773f-b4a4-52d1-99d4-7cb61e39d702" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-56" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139951/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ade66564-dcc9-5bc7-b541-cf2ce46c61b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-139951/selection/faf6532f0d4ab903ddc295ac11018acfd3bce2ae030f3f2eed578181eeb5e5e5" :answer-field/choices ["q-139951/selection/695792c47319cb1ed098a6d83038b7ad6d032838f9103d693bf346f1dc234ff8" "q-139951/selection/faf6532f0d4ab903ddc295ac11018acfd3bce2ae030f3f2eed578181eeb5e5e5" "q-139951/selection/ebfc0e0786b9e08f32fe2539ae50e791a60b7c4613bb2a0820cefbd3ea742454" "q-139951/selection/bdda2450817a39aa33f63c44268d508ac25aa607d31de284a7a3098288a61525" "q-139951/selection/95f0217cc1a787fa427ae3652ee08f6e7e92976368d3018500a5edad740eb418"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-139951" :question/id #uuid "54ff819f-c769-5521-bdf5-51f70981bea2" :question/math-academy-id "q-139951" :question/problem "If $\\alpha \\beta =-8$ and $b\\cdot a=\\frac{15}{2}$, then what is $(\\alpha a)\\cdot (\\beta b)+12?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that the dot product is linear in both variables, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\alpha a)\\cdot (\\beta b)+12 & =\\alpha (a\\cdot \\beta b)+12 \\\\  & =\\alpha \\beta (a\\cdot b)+12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using that the dot product is symmetric, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha \\beta (a\\cdot b)+12 & =\\alpha \\beta (b\\cdot a)+12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $\\alpha \\beta $ and $b\\cdot a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha \\beta (b\\cdot a)+12 & =(-8)\\cdot \\frac{15}{2}+12 \\\\  & =-60+12 \\\\  & =-48\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-139951/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fba8401-2da1-50f2-8e96-84cbe06d95fc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-139951"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74041/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer/id #uuid "997a236a-1437-575f-a06d-6c9403e83723" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74041/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "9eba187a-411b-58bd-8a50-30ce5e8247ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74041/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" :answer/id #uuid "8e596a70-57c8-517c-89e1-33beae96be79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74041/selection/b556bb502f914dc4fab0f40312f13f23b29e033ef49212306202180f04718e6f" :answer/id #uuid "be15516d-6c2f-57d8-b4eb-0b93a11c95e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-22" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74041/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "d7ee2a66-646a-5dcd-a39a-5e1d2a74818d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74041/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7298328f-342e-5fe8-a5ba-da2f64db91d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74041/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer-field/choices ["q-74041/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" "q-74041/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-74041/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" "q-74041/selection/b556bb502f914dc4fab0f40312f13f23b29e033ef49212306202180f04718e6f" "q-74041/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74041" :question/id #uuid "f9ad90f2-46d9-558b-96c2-0fbbeabd4cb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-74041" :question/problem "Find $(3a-4b)\\cdot c+(2b)\\cdot d,$ if $c\\cdot a=-2,$ $c\\cdot b=4,$ and $d\\cdot b=5.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that the dot product is linear in the first variable, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3a-4b)\\cdot c+(2b)\\cdot d & =(3a)\\cdot c-(4b)\\cdot c+(2b)\\cdot d \\\\  & =3(a\\cdot c)-4(b\\cdot c)+2(b\\cdot d).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we can use the fact that the dot product is symmetric to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(a\\cdot c)-4(b\\cdot c)+2(b\\cdot d) & =3(c\\cdot a)-4(c\\cdot b)+2(d\\cdot b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the values for $c\\cdot a,$ $c\\cdot b$ and $d\\cdot b,$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(c\\cdot a)-4(c\\cdot b)+2(d\\cdot b) & =3(-2)-4(4)+2(5) \\\\  & =-6-16+10 \\\\  & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $(3a-4b)\\cdot c+(2d)\\cdot b=-12.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-74041/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fba8401-2da1-50f2-8e96-84cbe06d95fc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74041"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-39202"] :question/problem "Find $(3a+b)\\cdot c+(2b-2c)\\cdot d,$ if $c\\cdot a=3,$ $c\\cdot b=-2,$ $b\\cdot d=-1,$ and $d\\cdot c=2.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the fact that the dot product is linear in the first variable, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3a+b)\\cdot c+(2b-2c)\\cdot d & =(3a)\\cdot c+b\\cdot c+(2b)\\cdot d-(2c)\\cdot d \\\\  & =3(a\\cdot c)+b\\cdot c+2(b\\cdot d)-2(c\\cdot d).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we can use the fact that the dot product is symmetric to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(a\\cdot c)+b\\cdot c+2(b\\cdot d)-2(c\\cdot d) & =3(c\\cdot a)+c\\cdot b+2(b\\cdot d)-2(d\\cdot c).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the values for $c\\cdot a,$ $c\\cdot b,$ $b\\cdot d,$ and $d\\cdot c,$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(c\\cdot a)+c\\cdot b+2(b\\cdot d)-2(d\\cdot c) & =3(3)+(-2)+2(-1)-2(2) \\\\  & =9-2-2-4 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $(3a+b)\\cdot c+(2b-2c)\\cdot d=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-40049/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "eb9586c2-2d08-57b9-ae55-ebd1c9aa7f7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40049/selection/845beb42e162b04150b7b438e2c57c85fb9c5dc5bb6c7f2891f90687bf6